rt enters all 20 recording windows as independent trials in an exact binomial sign test (binomtest(n_lower=15, n=20)) while itself stating only 6 gearboxes are represented; workflow/analysis.py performs no per-gearbox aggregation or cluster adjustment, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit are fed into a row-independent procedure as if independent — the issue is demonstrated in the selected report.\",\"The marginal significance (p = 0.0414 < 0.05) depends on the inflated n of 20 clustered rows rather than the 6 independent units, so the stated rejection of the 50% null rests directly on the demonstrated independence violation.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column gearbox_id exists in data/input.csv and repeats across rows exactly as described (20 windows clustered in 6 gearboxes: G-14 x4, G-21 x3, G-33 x4, G-47 x3, G-52 x3, G-68 x3); both procedure arms (baseline_floor_db, adaptive_floor_db) are paired per-row measurements governed by the same unit column, so the declaration is consistent with the frozen data.","The selected report enters all 20 recording windows as independent trials in an exact binomial sign test (binomtest(n_lower=15, n=20)) while itself stating only 6 gearboxes are represented; workflow/analysis.py performs no per-gearbox aggregation or cluster adjustment, so repeated measurements from the same independent unit are fed into a row-independent procedure as if independent — the issue is demonstrated in the selected report.","The marginal significance (p = 0.0414 < 0.05) depends on the inflated n of 20 clustered rows rather than the 6 independent units, so the stated rejection of the 50% null rests directly on the demonstrated independence violation.","No authority lock was minted, so lock_f